    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.11), who represent our strongest plays. **Cole Carrigg** benefits from a rare intersection of a favorable hitters' park and a targetable matchup against Robbie Ray, while **Kyle Tucker** remains an auto-start despite a modest platoon drop-off, given his elite floor. **Heliot Ramos** also projects as a top-tier asset (70.57) today; he is in a prime spot against Sean Sullivan, whose 6.43 xERA is the most exploitable mark on our board. We are aggressively leveraging these favorable SP matchups to maximize our 5x5 categories, particularly leaning on the speed and contact upside of **Andy Pages**, who draws a +13% boost from his matchup against Wandy Peralta.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the rotation was benching **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.46), who sits just outside the starting threshold. Despite his pedigree, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faced a significant projected efficiency drag against Logan Gilbert, pushing him behind the higher-scoring profiles of **Josh Jung** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, the latter of whom benefits from a +14% dynamic platoon advantage. Managing these edges is critical, especially with the high-stakes 5x5 format where every stolen base counts; we are monitoring the 42% rain risk looming over **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 64.31 score is contingent on him clearing the weather. While **Brayan Rocchio** holds a spot at 45.94, his involvement remains sensitive to the 37% rain risk in his contest; we are keeping **Miguel Vargas** on high alert on the bench should the lineups shift or weather force a late-inning pivot.",
